// REJECTED - item 378: a config field whose declared type REACHES an arrow.
//
// A config value is injected as static data at plug/spawn/load time, so a
// config field's declared type must be built, TRANSITIVELY, out of data. An
// arrow field is a live callable the body can invoke past every authority
// fold: no ticket, no reach attribution, no `emission[...]` bound to exceed.
//
// The indirection is the point. `Hooks` is a record of data except for one
// field, so nothing about the type as WRITTEN (`hooks: Hooks`) says anything
// is wrong - the refusal only exists once the declaration is resolved and
// descended into. Reading the spelling is not enough; a checker, or a model
// of one, has to walk.
//
// Everything else here is accepted: drop `tail` from `Hooks` and the file
// compiles, so the only refusal this fixture carries is the config one.
//
// This is the fixture the formal harness grew its config-is-data row for
// (issue 1161). The model's two other G4 rules both judge a CROSSING -
// `Oracle.g4OK` the emission marker, `Oracle.hostAcquireOK` the acquire
// bracket - and there is no crossing here to judge: the offence is in a
// DECLARED TYPE, which is a fact of a kind the export did not carry. Until it
// did, this refusal read as `missed-G4` wherever the file was put, since
// `diff_corpus.CORPUS_DIRS` is `("examples", "tck", "tests")` and the fatal
// followed the file into every one of them.
//
// expected error:
//   config field `hooks` of component `Loader` has type `Hooks`, which
//   reaches an arrow (function) type; a config field must be static data

type Hooks = { head: Str, tail: (Str) -> Str }

service Sink {
  emission[log] fn write(row: Str) -> Int
}

component Loader requires log: Sink provides out: Sink {
  config { source: Str, hooks: Hooks }

  provide out {
    fn write(row) {
      emit log.write(row)
      return 1
    }
  }
}
